<title>SPAIN: TABLE - Breakdown of Spain's July jobless figures.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Breakdown of Spain's July jobless figures.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of Spain's July unemployment data compared with one month earlier, according to data provided by the Labour Ministry on Wednesday:</p>
<p>		     Fall in unemployed   Pct fall</p>
<p>BY SECTOR:</p>
<p>    Agriculture			5,061  8.29 pct</p>
<p>    Industry			  11,624  2.92 pct</p>
<p>    Construction		     7,913  3.36 pct</p>
<p>    Services			  42,116  4.21 pct</p>
<p>    New jobs (all sectors)	15,980  4.01 pct</p>
<p>BY SEX:</p>
<p>    Male				44,899  4.73 pct</p>
<p>(jobless rate  9.20 pct)</p>
<p>    Female			    37,795  3.31 pct</p>
<p>(jobless rate 17.72 pct)</p>
<p>BY AGE:</p>
<p>    25 and under		    28,925  6.53 pct</p>
<p>(jobless rate 15.78 pct)</p>
<p>    25 and over		     53,769  3.26 pct</p>
<p>BY REGION:</p>
<p>    Andalusia			 18,916</p>
<p>    Valencia			   9,168</p>
<p>    Galicia			    8,389</p>
<p>    Madrid			     7,986</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
